@@ -20,7 +20,7 @@ guardrail command map.
 | --- | --- | --- |
 | `start` | Read-only operator entry point: run doctor, optionally create a linked Quest draft, lint it, and return the stable structured next action. It never seals or begins work. | `node scripts/solve.js start --id <id> [--statement "<sealed result>" --class product|process --spec-ref <ref>] [--json]` |
 | `continue` | Execute only trusted structured begin/commit action codes from the current next projection. A commit summary automatically captures the canonical working-tree delta against the active source epoch; explicit --changeRef remains an exceptional compatibility path. Rendered command text and judgment/gate actions are never executed. | `node scripts/solve.js continue --id <id> [--summary "<what changed>"] [--changeRef diff:<path>] [--json]` |
-| `land` | For source work, freeze the exact terminal candidate and aggregate into an immutable review id; a later verdict by that id is drift-checked, recorded as a structured receipt, and on approval passed through the audit-gated scope-safe commit. Rejection never commits and requires category-complete findings; no path pushes. | `node scripts/solve.js land --id <id> [--review review-<hex> --verifier <stable-id> --verdict approve|reject --receipt <ref> [--finding "<category>: <summary>" ...]] [--json]` |
+| `land` | For source work, freeze one immutable review envelope containing the exact candidate/aggregate, source epoch, staged landing evidence, additive template checklist, generated-dependency receipts, and deterministic proof plan. A later structured verdict is drift-checked and ingested; approval passes through the audit-gated scope-safe commit, rejection never commits, and no path pushes. | `node scripts/solve.js land --id <id> [--review review-<hex> --verdict-file <workspace-receipt.json>] [--json]` |
 | `decompose-rejection` | Discharge a slice of a standing candidate rejection with fresh independently approved coverage: the current quest's exactly approved candidate, or a successor quest's candidate receipt that still matches current bytes at an acceptable base. Records an append-only rejection-decomposition event; the standing obligation shrinks to the uncovered remainder, so split scope stays dischargeable. | `node scripts/solve.js decompose-rejection --id <id> [--from-quest <successorId>]` |
 | `new` | Create a versioned Quest draft under solve/quests/<id>.json. Drafting is not sealing: the first execution command lints and declares it. Link flags author the planning graph without hand-editing JSON; --force is refused once append-only history exists. | `node scripts/solve.js new --id <id> --statement "<sealed result>" [--class product|process] [--plan-doc <path>] [--parent-quest <id>] [--roadmap-row <id>] [--spec-ref <ref>] [--closes-cl <CL-id>] [--inherit-rulesout-from <parentQuestId>]` |
 | `run` | Run the Quest loop toward SOLVED/EXHAUSTED. Bare `run --id <id>` uses the default `dry` executor (a no-op skeleton — it prints a banner saying so); real autonomous work needs `--executor agent --yes`. Add `--keep-alive` to replay only progress-bearing MAX_CYCLES boundaries; judgment and repair stops return once with a typed action. | `node scripts/solve.js run --id <id> --executor agent --yes --keep-alive [--max 20]` |
@@ -43,7 +43,7 @@ guardrail command map.
 | `reflect` | Record a reflection think-cycle (no attempt, no metric claim): micro by default, or `--altitude` to question the frame. `--note` is required. | `node scripts/solve.js reflect --id <id> --note "<text>" [--frontier <fid>] [--altitude]` |
 | `step` | Begin a supervised attempt: pins the frontier and prints the rung dossier. Records nothing until `--commit` (or `--abort` to discard the pending attempt). At commit time, `--auto-diff` snapshots `git diff` against the pin recorded at step begin into solve/changes/<id>/attempt-<n>.diff and uses it as the changeRef (errors if nothing changed; solver-generated bookkeeping — solve/FRONTIER.generated.md, solve/state, solve/log, solve/report — is excluded from the snapshot; an explicit --changeRef takes precedence and prints a warning that --auto-diff was ignored). | `node scripts/solve.js step --id <id> [--commit (--changeRef diff:<path> | --auto-diff) --summary "<what changed>" | --abort]` |
 | `step-pending` | Print the pending supervised step (the pinned baseline attempt awaiting a commit) as JSON. | `node scripts/solve.js step-pending --id <id>` |
